    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0844" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/3–2850: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Egypt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d420-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-03-28T18:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1950—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>256. Dept disturbed by press reports Arab League planning expel Jordan and by
                    Egypt-Saudi recommendation to this effect described Baghdad tel 208 Mar
                        28<anchor n="2" xml:id="d420-f2"/> rptd you as 38.</p>
                <p>Ref instrs contained Deptel 228 Mar 17<anchor n="3" xml:id="d420-f3"/> re Arab
                    interference in Jordan-Israeli relationship, Dept desires Emb in its discretion urge Egyptian Govt adopt
                    prudent and conciliatory approach to Jordan question in Arab League mtg.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d420-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d420-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated to other Arab capitals.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d420-f2" n="2" xml:id="d420-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d420-f3" n="3" xml:id="d420-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted to Cairo the text of telegram 95, March 17, to
                    Damascus, with instruction to take the action outlined in the last paragraph of
                    No. 95, if circumstances warranted (684A.85/3–1450). Ambassador Caffery, in
                    reply on March 25, stated he had “lectured” the Egyptian Foreign Minister the
                    previous day, “counseling moderation in general and in re Jordan in particular
                    at the Arab League Council meetings which begin today. He said that my advice
                    was sound and he would follow it.” (Telegram 286 from Cairo, 786.00/3–2550)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
